Do you want to shape how millions of members experience Basic-Fit, from the first email to the daily workout in the app? Are you excited to support a data-driven culture and to turn complex data into actionable insights? Can you spot the real story in your analyses and translate it into business opportunities? And do you love using AI to work smarter and faster? Our CRM team is expanding and we are looking for a CRM & App Data Analyst.

This Is What Your Role Looks Like

As part of our agile, multidisciplinary CRM team, you will support the continuous improvement of our member journeys. You will analyse campaign performance and member behaviour across CRM channels and the Basic-Fit app. The app is a core part of the member journey, so you will make sure it gets the same analytical attention as our campaigns. You will translate your analyses into valuable business insights and share recommendations with business owners. You will use AI as a natural part of how you work, for example to speed up analyses, explore data and automate recurring reporting.

Your Responsibilities

* Deliver high-quality analyses on campaign performance, member behavior and app engagement;
* Design and develop dashboards and reports (Power BI, Looker Studio) that combine CRM, app and other data sources;
* Prepare, execute and analyze A/B tests across CRM campaigns and the app;
* Define and manage app event tracking (Google Analytics/Firebase) together with the app team, so the data you need is accurate and complete;
* Collaborate with the Data Platform Team to bring missing data into our central Data Platform (Databricks);
* Apply AI tools to work more efficiently and to find new ways to generate insights, and share what works with your colleagues;
* Contribute to various projects of the CRM team, from design to evaluation, and define projects that support your own development.

This Is How Your Team Looks Like

You will be part of the CRM team, representing 5 nationalities, which core objective is to increase the value of our members by ensuring they stay happy members for as long possible:

* Root-cause analysis, KPI setting and dashboarding;
* Business partnering with the international leadership team;
* End-to-end development of (self-service) business intelligence;
* (Financial) management and board reporting.

Within your role you are fully assigned to the success of the CRM team, and you work closely with the app development team, data scientists and data engineers. On a recurring basis, all data analysts share their knowledge and analyses on their domains.

Who Are You?

An analytical thinker with a business-driven attitude and the capacity to digest complex information, see trends and insights in data, and translate them into concrete actions. A self-starter, strong team player and proven problem solver with good stakeholder management and communication skills.

* Relevant Bachelor's/Master's degree (HBO/WO);
* At least 1-3 years of relevant experience;
* Proficiency in SQL and hands-on experience with the Microsoft BI stack (DAX, Power BI, Azure);
* Hands-on experience with app and event tracking, preferably Google Analytics, Firebase and Google Tag Manager;
* Experience with data platforms and languages such as Databricks, BigQuery, Python/R and PySpark is a benefit;
* Marketing (Cloud) knowledge is a benefit;
* Experience with Git is a benefit;
* Curiosity about and practical experience with AI tools in your daily work, combined with a critical eye for the quality and reliability of their output;
* You want to keep developing in the newest technologies.

What We Offer You

At Basic-Fit, it’s not just about work, it’s about your growth. As a CRM and App Data Analyst, you’ll have the freedom to make an impact and develop yourself in a dynamic environment.

What you can expect from us:

* Learning & Development: Unlimited access to GoodHabitz and LinkedIn Learning.
* Career Growth: Plenty of opportunities for professional and personal development.
* Work Culture: An informal, international, and down-to-earth environment. We value working together, so we work 4 days in the office, 1 day from home.
* Innovation: Your ideas contribute to strategic projects.
* Salary: A monthly gross salary between €3500 and €4800 based on 40 hours, depending on your experience and background.
* Perks & Benefits: Travel allowance, pension plan, bike plan, health insurance discounts and remote work allowance.
* Fitness: Access to our gym at HQ.

About Basic-Fit

Basic-Fit is Europe's leader in the value-for-money fitness market, with more than 5+ million members across 2,000+ clubs in 7 countries. We are continuously growing and improving. If you're looking for a place where you can make an impact while having fun at work, you've come to the right place!

What Makes Us Unique?

* Work with Impact: What you do makes a difference. We don’t just work for our members, partners, and teams—we work with them.
* Collaboration: Everyone works together to achieve goals and celebrate success.
* Diversity & Inclusion: We welcome everyone into our workplace.

Apply Now!

Ready for your next adventure? Click the Apply button, and we’ll get in touch with you as soon as possible.

Questions? Feel free to contact Kerensa at kerensa.vanderlans@basic-fit.com.

